        opening_activity: 'Thought Trap share: who caught a trap? What was the Talk Back? Celebrate the effort.',
        main_activity: 'Introduce the Worry Ladder (exposure concept in kid-friendly terms). "When you avoid something scary, your worry brain thinks: See! I was right! It WAS dangerous! And the fear grows. But when you take small brave steps toward the fear, your worry brain learns: Oh, this is actually OK." Draw a ladder on the board. Put the scariest version of a common fear at the top (giving a speech in front of the whole school) and the easiest brave step at the bottom (reading aloud to the counselor). Fill in the middle rungs together. Each student then creates their own Worry Ladder for ONE thing they avoid. Bottom rung = easiest step they could take this week.',
