        opening_activity: 'Profile update: what new fact did you add? Counselor highlights how a vague goal becomes real once a deadline is attached.',
        main_activity: 'Teach goal-setting that survives contact with real life: a goal should be specific, measurable, and have a deadline ("Apply to two welding programs by December 1" beats "get into a trade"). Each student writes one post-secondary goal in that format. Then they reverse-engineer it: working backward from the deadline, list every step (gather documents, request transcripts, ask for a recommendation, complete an application, look into aid, visit or tour) and assign each a target date. Students identify which steps depend on other people so they can start those early. Counselor circulates to make timelines realistic and to catch missing steps.',
